# ── Line endings ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Without this, what lands in a working copy depends on each contributor's
# core.autocrlf setting: the same file arrives LF on one machine and CRLF on
# another, and Git warns that it is about to convert it. `text=auto` makes the
# repository authoritative — every text file is stored with LF and checked out
# in the platform's native ending — so the warning has nothing left to warn
# about and no diff is ever just a line-ending change.
* text=auto

# Binary files Git must never convert, whatever content detection decides.
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.jpeg   binary
*.gif    binary
*.webp   binary
*.ico    binary
*.zip    binary
*.woff   binary
*.woff2  binary
*.ttf    binary
*.otf    binary
*.eot    binary
*.mo     binary

